WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.500 --> 00:00:08.260
Some video games are fun from start to finish.
Others seem to leave out the "finish" part

00:00:08.260 --> 00:00:12.410
and remain unbeatable forever. Here's a selection
of games that, for whatever reason, haven't

00:00:12.410 --> 00:00:16.680
been beaten by very many people. Maybe you'd
like to try?

00:00:16.680 --> 00:00:18.110
Battletoads

00:00:18.110 --> 00:00:22.190
Its difficulty is the stuff of myth. Many
claim to have beaten Battletoads without having

00:00:22.190 --> 00:00:26.640
any actual proof. The adventures of Rash,
Zitz, and Pimple were exceptionally challenging

00:00:26.640 --> 00:00:30.170
because you had to battle multiple streams
of bad guys, and you could accidentally punch

00:00:30.170 --> 00:00:34.949
your own teammate. It was completely possible
to keep dying because of friendly attacks.

00:00:34.949 --> 00:00:36.250
Harsh.

00:00:36.250 --> 00:00:37.680
Takeshi's Challenge

00:00:37.680 --> 00:00:42.950
Takeshi's Challenge gave fits to Japanese
Famicom fans. The "Takeshi" in question is

00:00:42.950 --> 00:00:46.910
actor/director Takeshi Kitano, a man who holds
the distinction of being one of the first

00:00:46.910 --> 00:00:50.320
celebrities to get involved with the world
of gaming. Sadly, his efforts produced what

00:00:50.320 --> 00:00:53.969
is wildly considered to be one of the worst
games of all time. Takeshi's Challenge is

00:00:53.969 --> 00:00:58.440
nearly unbeatable, largely because of gameplay
that pretty much depends on trial and error.

00:00:58.440 --> 00:01:01.379
There's even one section that requires the
use of the second controller's microphone

00:01:01.379 --> 00:01:06.130
to sing karaoke. While the game could be beaten
by suffering through the confusing gameplay,

00:01:06.130 --> 00:01:10.729
you could have also thrown 30,720 punches
on the opening screen to get to the ending.

00:01:10.729 --> 00:01:14.000
Say goodbye to your thumbs. And maybe your
mind.

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:15.540
Super Meat Boy

00:01:15.540 --> 00:01:20.140
Released in 2010, Super Meat Boy was created
as an intentional throwback to the crazy-hard

00:01:20.140 --> 00:01:23.750
games of our youth. And if you ask anyone
who's played it, it definitely delivers on

00:01:23.750 --> 00:01:27.659
that promise. There are tons of videos on
YouTube that show players dying over, and

00:01:27.659 --> 00:01:32.119
over, and over again. Needless to say, Super
Meat Boy is one of the hardest games released

00:01:32.119 --> 00:01:36.130
in recent memory, and fans love it for that
very reason. And while there are plenty of

00:01:36.130 --> 00:01:39.430
players that soldiered through the challenge
of beating the game, Steam's Global Gameplay

00:01:39.430 --> 00:01:43.960
stats list a measly two percent of players
have achieved 100 percent completion on it.

00:01:43.960 --> 00:01:47.180
Maybe they should rename this game "Super
Incomplete Boy."

00:01:47.180 --> 00:01:48.950
Friday the 13th

00:01:48.950 --> 00:01:53.079
As we mentioned, Super Meat Boy is an homage
to the tight, challenging games of yesteryear.

00:01:53.079 --> 00:01:56.390
But for every Metroid or Super Mario Bros.,
there are lots of other old games that were

00:01:56.390 --> 00:02:02.729
hard not because they were good, but because
they were bad. Very, very bad. Case in point:

00:02:02.729 --> 00:02:07.290
Friday the 13th for the original Nintendo
Entertainment System. In 2009, Game Informer

00:02:07.290 --> 00:02:11.140
magazine included this on its list of the
worst horror video games. Other magazines

00:02:11.140 --> 00:02:15.310
have gone a step further by calling Friday
the 13th one of the worst games ever made,

00:02:15.310 --> 00:02:20.190
period. Friday the 13th is very nearly impossible
to beat...but mostly because it's so crappy

00:02:20.190 --> 00:02:23.400
that most players would simply throw their
controllers through the TV before getting

00:02:23.400 --> 00:02:25.129
anywhere close to completing it.

00:02:25.129 --> 00:02:27.640
That still counts, right?

00:02:27.640 --> 00:02:29.480
Teenage Mutant Ninja Turtles

00:02:29.480 --> 00:02:33.360
Konami's Teenage Mutant Ninja Turtles game
deserves a special place on our list. Despite

00:02:33.360 --> 00:02:37.040
the fact that it gave players bald spots from
tearing their hair out in frustration, it

00:02:37.040 --> 00:02:41.300
was actually very popular at the time. Because
of impossible experiences like the ones provided

00:02:41.300 --> 00:02:45.410
by Teenage Mutant Ninja Turtles, we can fondly
look back on a time when games not only challenged

00:02:45.410 --> 00:02:49.910
us, but also extinguished our hope of finishing
them. Call it a sneak peek at the harsh realities

00:02:49.910 --> 00:02:50.690
of adult life.

00:02:50.690 --> 00:02:53.920
"Ooohhhhh noooo!"

00:02:53.920 --> 00:02:57.080
Thanks for watching! Subscribe to our YouTube
channel to watch more videos like the one

00:02:57.080 --> 00:03:00.500
you just saw. And leave us a comment to let
us know which game you think is unbeatable...

